-- title:
--   Function field comparison for the fake elliptic curve moduli curve
-- statement:
--   Fix a nonzero natural number $N$ and distinct primes $q,q'$, neither dividing $N$, and let $D$ be divisible by $2Nqq'$. Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ satisfy `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q q'`, i.e. $0<a$ or $0<b$, and for each height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ every nonzero element of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a unit exactly when $q\in v$ or $q'\in v$; let $\Lambda$ be a maximal $\mathbb Z$-order in $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$, let $N$ be squarefree, let $R\le\Lambda$ be an Eichler order of level $N$ (an intersection of two maximal orders, of relative index $N$ in the first), and let $\iota:\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\to M_2(\mathbb{R})$ be an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra map. Assume given an integral scheme $X$ with a morphism $\pi_X$ to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}[1/D]$ which is smooth, proper and smooth of relative dimension one with integral geometric fibres, together with a point rule `pt` sending each `FakeEllipticCurve Λ N S` over a ring $S$ with base point $s$ to an $X$-point over $s$, invariant under `FakeEllipticCurve.Iso`, compatible with pullbacks along ring maps, and inducing a bijection between isomorphism classes and points over algebraically closed fields. Let $F_0$ be a curve over $\mathbb C$ (in the sense of `IsCurveOver`), essentially of finite type, carrying a `UniformizedHeckeCurve` $U_0$ for `fuchsianGroup R ι` — the image in $GL_2(\mathbb R)$ of the group generated by the units of $R$, intersected with the kernel of the determinant — subject to the hypothesis bundle $h_0$: surjectivity of $U_0.\mathrm{pt}$; for each prime $\ell$, a finite set $S$ of elements of $R$ of reduced norm $\ell$ representing, uniquely up to left multiplication by units of $R$ of reduced norm $1$, the Hecke set `levelHeckeUSet Λ R ℓ` (if $\ell\mid N$) or `primeHeckeSet R ℓ` under $x\mapsto x\otimes 1$, with $U_0.\mathrm{heckePoints}\,\ell$ equal as a multiset to the image of $S$ under $\iota$; and the analytic clauses for $U_0.\mathrm{realize}$ (meromorphy at every point of the upper half-plane, additivity, multiplicativity, constancy on constants, germwise injectivity, invariance under the Fuchsian group, and realisation of every invariant meromorphic function) — these being summarised here. Let $s_{\mathbb C}$ be a $\mathbb C$-point of the base, $F_{\mathbb C}$ another essentially finite type curve over $\mathbb C$ with a `CurveModel` $\mathfrak M_{\mathbb C}$ whose underlying scheme is identified, by an isomorphism $e_{\mathfrak M}$ compatible with the structure morphisms, with the pullback of $\pi_X$ along $s_{\mathbb C}$. Assume further a map $\mathrm{per}_E$ from fake elliptic curves over $\mathbb C$ to the upper half-plane with $E\cong E'$ if and only if $U_0.\mathrm{pt}(\mathrm{per}_E E)=U_0.\mathrm{pt}(\mathrm{per}_E E')$ and with every $U_0.\mathrm{pt}(\tau)$ of this form, and a map $V:F_{\mathbb C}\to(\mathbb{H}\to\mathbb{C})$ whose values are meromorphic at every point and invariant under the Fuchsian group on punctured neighbourhoods, and which is additive, multiplicative and constant-preserving there. Finally assume that for every $x\in F_{\mathbb C}$, every place $\mathfrak P$ of $F_{\mathbb C}$ over $\mathbb C$ whose associated point corresponds under $e_{\mathfrak M}$ to the $\mathbb C$-point attached to $E$, and every $\tau$ with $U_0.\mathrm{pt}(\tau)=U_0.\mathrm{pt}(\mathrm{per}_E E)$, membership of $x$ in the valuation subring of $\mathfrak P$ is equivalent to boundedness of $\|V x\|$ along the punctured neighbourhood filter at $\tau$. Then there is a $\mathbb C$-algebra isomorphism $e:F_{\mathbb C}\to F_0$ such that for all $x$ and all $\tau$ the functions $U_0.\mathrm{realize}(e\,x)$ and $V x$ agree near $\tau$ off $\tau$, and such that for every place $\mathfrak P$ and every $E$ whose $\mathbb C$-point corresponds to $\mathfrak P$ as above, $e\,x$ lies in the valuation subring of $U_0.\mathrm{pt}(\mathrm{per}_E E)$ if and only if $x$ lies in that of $\mathfrak P$.
--
--   This is the algebraic half of Shimura's complex uniformisation of the coarse moduli curve of fake elliptic curves with Eichler level structure: granted a period map and a meromorphic realisation of the function field of the complex fibre, the function field is identified with the automorphic function field of the Fuchsian group, compatibly with places and with the moduli interpretation of points. It is combined with the construction of the period map and realisation in [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.exists_period_algEquiv_pt_iff_bcPlace_of_uniformizedHeckeCurve_of_two_mul_dvd`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.exists_period_algEquiv_pt_iff_bcPlace_of_uniformizedHeckeCurve_of_two_mul_dvd), and rests on the abstract comparison [`ModularCurve.UniformizedHeckeCurve.exists_algEquiv_realize_eventuallyEq_of_meromorphicAt_of_separatesOrbits`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UniformizedHeckeCurve.exists_algEquiv_realize_eventuallyEq_of_meromorphicAt_of_separatesOrbits).
